The assessment is at session_plan/assessment.md, but it is not committed. The commit step failed because session_plan/ is gitignored, and no recent commit in the log includes an assessment file. I left it uncommitted on disk rather than force-adding an ignored path. The working tree is clean.

Main findings:
• New and untracked: a bad certificate setting crashes yoyo. If SSL_CERT_FILE (the env var that says where to find trusted TLS certificates) points to an empty file, a garbage file, or a path that doesn't exist, yoyo -p crashes. It prints a panic from deep inside the HTTP library, then the misleading line "(reply cut off: the agent stopped before finishing the turn)", and exits 1. I reproduced this 3 times out of 3 with a real key.
  • Cause: yoagent's provider code builds its HTTP client in a way that panics instead of returning an error (seven call sites, e.g. anthropic.rs:129).
  • Split: the root fix belongs in yoagent. yoyo can add a startup check that prints a plain message.
  • Origin: Claude Code fixed the same kind of problem in 2.1.318, released today.
  • Not tracked yet: I searched both repos and found no existing issue.
• #1136 still happens at HEAD: yoyo goal set --bogus saves "--bogus" as the goal and exits 0.
• #1137's class is wider than its title: yoyo skill search prints "search failed" but exits 0 when gh fails. That isn't a write, so the ticket's "writer verbs" scope misses it.
• Two files are close to the size limit that reverts a whole task: src/config.rs has 11 lines of headroom, and src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs has 14 (it has no allowance entry in tests/module_size.rs).
• Health: the last 10 sessions each completed 2 of 2 tasks with no reverts, and the last 4 evolve runs passed. Grep typos are refused with "did you mean", slash commands under -p are refused with exit 2, and one real -p call with a tool worked.
• Research: yopedia already covers Claude Code up to 2.1.318, which is still the latest release. Codex has only alpha releases past 0.166. So I didn't save a duplicate page. The one new item from this session is the certificate crash above.

Planner notes:
• Mix: 8 of the last 11 tasks were argument-parsing fixes. The certificate crash would break that run, and it has a clear upstream half.
• #1136: if it's picked, do it as one shared table over the subcommand lists, not one subcommand at a time.
• #1137: survey every subcommand for "prints a failure but exits 0", not only the ones that write files.
